{
  "message": "I'm here to help you get your mobile data working as best as possible! To start, I'll guide you step by step. First, could you please provide your phone number or your full name and date of birth? This will help me identify your account and assist you better."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you, John. To help improve your mobile data speed, I'll guide you through a few steps. Let's start by making sure your phone is set to use the fastest available network. Please follow this instruction:

Set your network mode preference to '4G/5G Preferred'.

Let me know once you've done this, or if you need help with how to do it."
}

{
  "message": "Great job! Next, let's make sure nothing else is slowing down your connection. If you are using a VPN (Virtual Private Network), it can sometimes make your internet slower. Please disconnect your VPN if it is currently connected.\n\nLet me know once you've done this, or if you need help with how to disconnect your VPN."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for disconnecting the VPN. Now, let's make sure your mobile data is turned ON. Please check your phone's settings and ensure that mobile data is enabled. If it is off, please turn it ON.\n\nLet me know once you've done this, or if you need help with how to turn on mobile data."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for turning on mobile data. Next, let's make sure that Data Saver mode is not limiting your speed. Please check if Data Saver mode is ON, and if it is, turn it OFF.\n\nLet me know once you've done this, or if you need help with how to turn off Data Saver mode."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. I checked your account and noticed that you had already used all the data included in your plan, which can cause your internet to slow down or stop working. I have just added 2GB of extra data to your line for $4.00, so your internet should now work much better.\n\nPlease try using your mobile data again and let me know if you notice an improvement. If you still don't get excellent speed, let me know and we can continue troubleshooting together."
}

{
  "message": "I'm here to help, and I understand how important this is for you. Let's check a few more things to get your connection working. First, please check if Airplane Mode is turned ON by mistake. If it is, please turn it OFF.\n\nLet me know once you've checked this, or if you need help with how to check Airplane Mode."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for turning off Airplane Mode. Now, please try using your mobile data again to see if your internet connection is working. If it is still not working or not as fast as you expect, please let me know, and we will continue troubleshooting together until your connection is excellent."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience, and I'm sorry this is still not working. Let's check if your SIM card is being recognized by your phone. Please check your SIM card status in your phone's settings. If it shows as missing or not detected, try removing and reinserting the SIM card. Let me know what your phone says about the SIM card status, or if you need help with how to check this."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking your SIM card status. Since your SIM card is active, let's check your phone's APN (Access Point Name) settings next. Please look at your APN settings and see if anything looks incorrect or if the MMSC URL is missing. If you're not sure, you can reset your APN settings to default. After resetting, please restart your phone for the changes to take effect.\n\nLet me know once you've done this, or if you need help with how to reset your APN settings."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for sharing your APN settings. Resetting your APN settings will only change your network connection settings—it will not delete any of your photos, messages, or personal data. It is safe to do and can often fix internet connection issues.\n\nPlease go ahead and reset your APN settings to default, then restart your phone. Let me know once you've done this, or if you need help with how to reset your APN settings."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. I see that your line is active, your SIM card is working, and you have extra data available. Since your phone is also properly activated, let's try one more thing: please turn your phone off completely, wait about 30 seconds, and then turn it back on. This can help refresh your connection to the network.\n\nLet me know once you've restarted your phone and if your internet connection is working. If it still isn't, we will continue to help you until it's fixed."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your service issue. To get started, I need to verify your account. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for the information, John. To help diagnose why your phone is showing 'No Service', could you please check your phone's status bar and let me know what icons or messages you see at the top of your screen? This will help me determine if there are any issues like Airplane Mode being enabled or signal problems."
}

{
  "message": "Your line (555-123-2002) is currently suspended due to an overdue bill. I have just sent you a payment request for the overdue amount. Please check your payment requests and follow the instructions to complete the payment. Once the overdue bill is paid, I can help you restore your service."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for completing the payment. I have now restored your service. Please reboot your phone to regain signal and service. If you still see 'No Signal' after restarting, let me know and I can help you with further troubleshooting."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for letting me know. You will not lose your photos during this troubleshooting process. Let's continue to resolve your service issue. Next, I need to check the status of your SIM card. Could you please check your SIM card status on your phone and let me know if it says 'Active', 'Missing', or 'Locked'?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for checking. If your phone says there is no SIM card detected, it means your phone cannot connect to the network, which is why you have no service. This is usually not serious and can often be fixed by reseating the SIM card. Please remove your SIM card from your phone, wait a few seconds, and then reinsert it securely. After you have done this, let me know if your phone detects the SIM card or if you still see the same message."
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD ON."
}

{
  "message": "I can help you with your MMS issue. First, I need to verify your account for security purposes. Could you please provide either your phone number, customer ID, or your full name along with your date of birth?"
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for verifying your information, John. To help resolve your MMS issue, I’ll need to guide you through a few troubleshooting steps. First, please check if Wi-Fi Calling is enabled on your device, as this can sometimes interfere with MMS. Please use the toggle_wifi_calling() action to turn Wi-Fi Calling OFF, then let me know once you’ve done this."
}

{
  "message": "Great, thank you. The next step is to reset your phone's APN settings, as incorrect APN settings can often cause MMS issues. Please use the reset_apn_settings() action on your device. Let me know once you have completed this step."
}

{
  "message": "Perfect. For the changes to take effect, please reboot your device now by using the reboot_device() action. Once your phone has restarted, try sending an MMS message again and let me know if the issue is resolved."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for your patience. Let's check if your mobile data is enabled, as MMS requires mobile data to work. Please use the toggle_data() action to ensure your mobile data is turned ON. After enabling mobile data, try sending an MMS again and let me know if it works."
}

{
  "message": "Thank you for trying that. The next step is to reseat your SIM card, as SIM card issues can sometimes cause problems with sending MMS. Please use the reseat_sim_card() action on your device. Once you've done this, try sending an MMS again and let me know if it works."
}

